iven below?\n\n- $E$ is a singular matrix\n- $E$ is **not**  a singular matrix\n- $det(E)=-2$\n\n$$\nE=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & 3 & 4 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & 5 & 6 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & 7 & 8\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139536082 true] [17592186382717 1113 #uuid "08581ff2-f136-5cd3-82eb-06aac34673a0" 13194139536082 true] [17592186382717 1145 "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(E) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & 3 & 4 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & 5 & 6 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & 7 & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}|\\begin{aligned}5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 8\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & 6 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & 8\\end{aligned}|+4|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & 5 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(40-42)-3(\\frac{16}{3}-\\frac{12}{3})+4(\\frac{14}{3}-\\frac{10}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot (-2)-3\\cdot \\frac{4}{3}+4\\cdot \\frac{4}{3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}-\\frac{12}{3}+\\frac{16}{3} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(E)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statement I is true." 13194139536082 true] [17592186382718 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382719 13194139536082 true] [17592186382718 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382720 13194139536082 true] [17592186382718 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382721 13194139536082 true] [17592186382718 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382722 13194139536082 true] [17592186382718 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382723 13194139536082 true] [17592186382718 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536082 true] [17592186382718 1041 "selection" 13194139536082 true] [17592186382718 1104 #edb/ref 17592186382720 13194139536082 true] [17592186382718 1110 #uuid "14fc5fd3-acb1-5e2d-848c-f71765f05031" 13194139536082 true] [17592186382719 1034 "II and III only" 13194139536082 true] [17592186382719 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536082 true